'''Ratnagiri''' is a port city on the [[Konkan]] coast of [[Maharashtra]], famous for Alphonso mangoes.

==Get in==
Ratnagiri station is on the [[Konkan Railway]].

==See==
{{see|name=Ratnadurg Fort|lat=16.9967|long=73.2728|content=Sea fort with a lighthouse and views of the harbour.}}
{{see|name=Thibaw Palace|lat=16.9870|long=73.2980|content=Built for the exiled last king of Burma.}}

==Eat==
Try ''Alphonso'' mangoes in season and a Malvani fish thali anywhere near the bus stand.

==Sleep==
{{sleep|name=MTDC Ganpatipule|lat=17.1450|long=73.2660|content=Beach resort 25 km north of the city.}}

